// ReadJobSensitive Read the one-time secret of a job result
//
// Requires `jobs.sensitive` (admins: any job of the organization; resellers and clients: the jobs they created). Returns the reserved `sensitive` member of a succeeded job's result (a generated WordPress administrator password) exactly once: the control plane keeps it only in process memory for 15 minutes and stores it nowhere. Every later call, another tenant's call, a call after the TTL and a call after a control plane restart answer 404. `Cache-Control: no-store`. The read is audited without the value.
//
// Corresponds with GET /jobs/{id}/sensitive (the `ReadJobSensitive` operationId).
