// Resolves the catalog image's `stable` tag to a manifest digest from the platform registry (server-side, at deploy time), stores the service (`deploying`) and enqueues `deploy_app_container` with the digest. When the account's runtime is not ready yet, `ensure_account_runtime` (with the account's CPU/memory limits) is enqueued first and the deploy follows when it succeeds; if it fails, the service becomes `failed` with the runtime error. The service becomes `running` when the agent reports success; live state, health, restarts and the published host address come from heartbeats (`live`).
