// DeleteUser Delete a user: pseudonymization (two steps)
//
// Requires `users.manage` (ADR-0013 §4). 1. Without `confirm_token`: 202 `{confirm_token, expires_at}` (`ppu1_…`, single use, 10 minutes, SHA-256 only). 2. With `?confirm_token=`: 200 `{user}`: status `deleted`, e-mail `deleted-<id>@invalid`, display name emptied; password, authenticator app, passkeys, recovery codes, known devices, tokens and sessions removed. The id stays and audit rows are untouched. Never oneself (409 `conflict`), never the last active admin (409 `last_admin`), never a reseller that owns accounts (409 `conflict`). Errors: 422 `confirm_token_invalid`, 409 `confirm_token_expired` / `confirm_token_used`. Audited `user.delete_requested` and `user.pseudonymized`.
